# What: Editor Files Block. Why: Editor and operating system settings belong to each machine, not the project. How: This ignores their folders and files.
*.njsproj
*.ntvs*
*.sln
*.suo
*.sw?
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode/*



# What: Log Files Block. Why: Logs are local run output, not source. How: This ignores the log files and logs folder, including the debug and error logs the package managers write.
*.log
lerna-debug.log*
logs
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*



# What: Generated And Local Files Block. Why: Build output, dependencies, local secrets, and tool state are recreated or kept per machine. How: This ignores the build and dev output, the bundled Netlify Functions, node_modules, local env files, the design folder's images and notes, the Claude and Playwright working folders, and the test suites' reports and run output.
*.env
*.local
.claude
.playwright
.playwright-cli
design/**
dev-dist/
dist
dist-ssr
netlify/functions
node_modules
tests/output



# What: Re-Include Block. Why: A shared file inside an ignored folder still belongs in the project, and a re-include only works after the pattern it overrides. How: This re-includes .vscode/extensions.json, so the editor's extension recommendations stay shared, and the design folder's folders, card templates, and render scripts, so the icons and preview cards can be rebuilt on another machine.
!.vscode/extensions.json
!design/**/
!design/**/*.html
!design/**/*.mts
